To handle a list of API calls in JavaScript using promises, you can use the `Promise.all` method. This method returns a promise that resolves to the list of results if all promises in the array are resolved. You can then use the `then` method to handle the results. Here's an example:

```javascript
const apiCalls = [
  'http://api1.com',
  'http://api2.com',
  'http://api3.com'
];

Promise.all(apiCalls).then(results => {
  console.log(results);
}).catch(error => {
  console.error(error);
});
```

In this example, the `Promise.all` method resolves to the list of results if all API calls are successful. The `then` method is used to handle the results, and the `catch` method is used to handle any errors that occur during the process.
